        "requirement": "Five drawers in the base",
        "status": "unmet",
        "evidence": "A drawer only fits on the cut face of a half base, and a half base has one cut face, so it holds one drawer (drawer:0#0,0#cut). A full base offered no drawer sockets, and neither did a quarter base. The only other drawer types (notch drawers and bays) need two or three bases touching, which the brief rules out. After the one drawer was fitted, find_sockets offered no more."
      }
    ],
    "summary": "A single base can't hold five drawers in this system: the most it takes is one. I swapped the full base for a north half base and put one drawer in its cut face. check_build reports no rule errors and the parts were checked for collisions and are clear. To get five drawers you'd need more bases, for example several half bases, or bases placed side by side for notch drawers and bays. That would go against the single-base requirement."
